  "term": "lurasidone",
  "definition": "Lurasidone is a second-generation antipsychotic medication commonly used in the context of schizophrenia and bipolar disorder. The source also notes that it is considered to have a relatively favorable metabolic profile, while its possible effects on development are not yet well understood.",
